{"name":"Incident with Actions, we are investigating reports of degraded availability","status":"resolved","created_at":"2026-05-06T07:19:07.862Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T17:13:58.724Z","monitoring_at":"2026-05-06T09:19:48.488Z","resolved_at":"2026-05-06T09:44:26.204Z","impact":"major","shortlink":"https://stspg.io/j22b66h0j5xl","scheduled_for":null,"scheduled_until":null,"scheduled_remind_prior":false,"scheduled_reminded_at":null,"impact_override":"major","scheduled_auto_in_progress":false,"scheduled_auto_completed":false,"metadata":{},"started_at":"2026-05-06T07:19:07.854Z","reminder_intervals":null,"id":"1qzncbrxcsy4","page_id":"kctbh9vrtdwd","incident_updates":[{"status":"resolved","body":"On May 6, 2026, from approximately 06:45 UTC to 09:15 UTC, GitHub Actions Standard Ubuntu hosted runners were degraded. 17.1% of jobs requesting a standard runner failed.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis was caused by an unexpected data shape in the allocation configuration data for standard runners. That data was introduced as part of post-incident remediation work for an incident the previous day and caused new allocations to be blocked as load ramped up for the day. Removing that data at 08:51 allowed allocations to proceed and hosted runner pools to scale up and recover.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWe are updating the filter logic for this allocation data to be resilient to abnormal data shapes and improving monitoring to alert when allocations are blocked, allowing the team to respond before customer impact starts.","created_at":"2026-05-06T09:44:26.204Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-05-08T17:13:58.720Z","display_at":"2026-05-06T09:44:26.204Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"j21d3v6ssmr6","incident_id":"1qzncbrxcsy4","custom_tweet":null,"affected_components":[{"code":"br0l2tvcx85d","name":"Actions","old_status":"operational","new_status":"operational"}]},{"status":"monitoring","body":"Actions wait times have fully recovered.","created_at":"2026-05-06T09:44:17.265Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-05-06T09:44:17.265Z","display_at":"2026-05-06T09:44:17.265Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"5tqh348lnknj","incident_id":"1qzncbrxcsy4","custom_tweet":null,"affected_components":[{"code":"br0l2tvcx85d","name":"Actions","old_status":"operational","new_status":"operational"}]},{"status":"monitoring","body":"The degradation affecting Actions has been mitigated. We are monitoring to ensure stability.","created_at":"2026-05-06T09:19:48.488Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-05-06T09:19:48.488Z","display_at":"2026-05-06T09:19:48.488Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"sp1pvlvzj9rz","incident_id":"1qzncbrxcsy4","custom_tweet":null,"affected_components":[{"code":"br0l2tvcx85d","name":"Actions","old_status":"partial_outage","new_status":"operational"}]},{"status":"investigating","body":"We've applied a mitigation to fix the issues with queuing and running Actions jobs. We are seeing improvements in telemetry and are monitoring for full recovery.","created_at":"2026-05-06T09:08:07.350Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-05-06T09:08:07.350Z","display_at":"2026-05-06T09:08:07.350Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"6g6226qvxt5d","incident_id":"1qzncbrxcsy4","custom_tweet":null,"affected_components":[{"code":"br0l2tvcx85d","name":"Actions","old_status":"partial_outage","new_status":"partial_outage"}]},{"status":"investigating","body":"Actions is experiencing issues with ubuntu standard hosted runners leading to high wait times. We are actively investigating the issue","created_at":"2026-05-06T08:00:18.919Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-05-06T08:00:18.919Z","display_at":"2026-05-06T08:00:18.919Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"g0gjh5zwdqqh","incide